Reviewed r3 at `ea0ad590`, read-only. Four of the six items pass. The selective registry and deterministic instrumentation fixes are sound, and table rebuilding can enforce the proposed constraints. However, D0’s upgrader is still not implementable as specified and would discard or invalidate supported schema artifacts.

## Re-verification

| Finding | Verdict | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| DP-r2-01 | **PASS** | r3 replaces nullable retrofits with `NOT NULL` and table-level `UNIQUE`, rebuilding existing `facts` and `ticks` tables ([design-proposal.md:119](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:119)). These schemas contain ordinary columns, checks, primary keys, and indexes, with no foreign keys ([sqlite_store.py:308](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:308)); therefore the proposed create/copy/drop/rename mechanism can enforce both constraints. The raw-SQL gate correctly proves table-level enforcement ([design-proposal.md:529](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceD/design-proposal.md:529)). Fresh-eyes caveats about other schema objects are DP-r3-02 below. |
